# Request Information

**For hospital executives, clinical champions, digital health leads, and procurement teams.**

We are happy to provide a scoping conversation, an information pack, or specific documentation to support your assessment. No commitment is implied by making an enquiry.

---

## What you can request

### Pilot discussion
A 30-minute conversation to explore whether Aescia is a fit for your discharge pathway. We will ask about your service, your cohort of interest, and your governance context. You will get an honest assessment of whether and how a pilot would work.

**Contact:** james@aesciahealth.com
**Subject line suggestion:** Pilot discussion — [your health service]

---

### Information pack
A concise overview document covering what Aescia is, how it works, what a pilot involves, and what it requires from a health service. Suitable for circulating to clinical governance, digital health, or executive leads ahead of a more detailed conversation.

**Includes:**
- One-page platform overview
- Pilot outline summary
- Governance and data handling summary
- Evaluation framework outline

**Contact:** james@aesciahealth.com
**Subject line suggestion:** Information pack request

---

### Security and governance documentation
For digital health, IT security, or procurement teams conducting a formal assessment.

**Available on request:**
- Security architecture overview
- Data governance summary
- Privacy impact assessment template
- Software development lifecycle summary
- Platform risk assessment
- Incident response procedure summary
- Draft data sharing agreement

These documents are provided under a standard information-sharing arrangement appropriate to the assessment context.

**Contact:** james@aesciahealth.com
**Subject line suggestion:** Security/governance documentation — [your health service]

---

### Frequently asked procurement questions
A compiled document addressing the questions most commonly asked by digital health procurement and governance teams. Covers classification, data handling, integration requirements, evaluation evidence, and regulatory posture.

**Contact:** james@aesciahealth.com
**Subject line suggestion:** Procurement FAQ request

---

## What to include in your enquiry

To help us respond usefully, please include:

- Your role and health service (or organisation type if not a hospital)
- The clinical area or discharge pathway you are considering
- What stage you are at — early exploration, formal assessment, or active planning
- Any specific constraints or requirements (privacy, hosting, integration, ethics process)
- Preferred response format (document, call, or both)

